  "id": "COMPOUND:16590 - PROTEIN:5754",
  "verbalization": "Gerontoisoflavone A appears to exert its biological effects through multiple distinct pathways, all ultimately targeting HSVEC. The first pathway involves the atypical kinase COQ8A, mitochondrial, which is targeted by a quinoline compound, and this kinase is predicted to interact with HSVEC. The second pathway links Gerontoisoflavone A to ATP-citrate synthase, which is targeted by K-252a, and this enzyme is also predicted to interact with HSVEC. The third pathway connects Gerontoisoflavone A to the serine/threonine-protein kinase TNNI3K, which is also targeted by K-252a and interacts with HSVEC. These findings suggest that Gerontoisoflavone A may act through different molecular mechanisms, each potentially modulating HSVEC through distinct pathways. The shared target of K-252a across these pathways implies a possible functional overlap, while the unique targets of Gerontoisoflavone A highlight its diverse pharmacological profile. The integration of these evidence points supports the hypothesis that Gerontoisoflavone A may influence HSVEC through multiple, yet interconnected, molecular mechanisms.",
